hadiths[116]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7748","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No woman should ask for the divorce of her sister in order to overturn what is in her bowl, for her provision is only upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic.""**"
"7749","ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb with one pronouncement, then took her back."
"7750","Anas رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah, then took her back."
"7751","Anas رضي الله عنه reported: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah, he was commanded to take her back in marriage."
"7752","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: ʿUmar entered upon Ḥafṣah رضي الله عنها while she was weeping and said to her, ""What makes you weep? Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced you. He already divorced you once before, then took you back for my sake. By Allah, if he divorces you another time, I will never speak to you again."""
"7753","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Ḥafṣah. When that reached ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, he put dust upon his head and said, ""What regard does Allah have for you, O son of al-Khaṭṭāb, after this?"" Then Jibrīl عليه السلام descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: > **""Allah commands you to take Ḥafṣah back, out of mercy for ʿUmar.""**"
"7754","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no divorce except after marriage, and no freeing except after ownership.""**"
"7755","Muʿādh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no divorce for one who has no authority over it, and no freeing for one who owns nothing.""**"
"7756","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""There is no marriage except after divorce.""**"
"7757","ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib رضي الله عنه said: I memorized six things for you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""There is no divorce except after marriage, no freeing except after ownership, no fulfilling a vow involving disobedience, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence from day until night, and no continuous fasting without breaking it.""**"
"7758","ʿIṣmah رضي الله عنه said: A slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my master married me off, and now he wishes to separate me from my wife."" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: > **""O people, divorce belongs only to the one who takes hold of the leg.""**"
"7759","Ibn Jurayj said: It reached Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما that Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه was saying, ""If a man divorces a woman he has not yet married, it is valid."" So Ibn ʿAbbās said, ""He erred in this. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: 'When you marry believing women and then divorce them before you have touched them' [Al-Aḥzāb: 49]. He did not say: when you divorce believing women and then marry them."""
"7760","Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān al-Jawzī said: I asked ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ about a man who mentions a woman and says, ""The day I marry her, she is divorced irrevocably."" ʿAṭāʾ said, ""There is no divorce for one who does not possess the marriage tie, and no freeing for one who does not own the slave."" This was attributed to Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما, who traced it to the Prophet ﷺ."
"7761","Abū Mūsā رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Women are not to be divorced except for misgiving. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not love the men who taste often nor the women who taste often.""**"
"7762","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه said: > **""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not love the men who taste often, nor the women who taste often.""**"
"7763","Jābir رضي الله عنه reported: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my wife does not withhold the hand of one who touches."" He ﷺ said: > **""Divorce her.""** The man said, ""I love her, and she is beautiful."" He ﷺ said: > **""Then enjoy her company.""**"
"7764","Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn said: Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما proposed to the daughter of Manṣūr ibn Sayyār ibn Rayyān al-Fazārī. He said, ""By Allah, I will marry you to him, though I know he is ardent, oft-divorcing, and oft-separating—except that he is of the noblest house among the Arabs and the noblest lineage."""
"7765","Fuḍālah ibn ʿUbayd al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: > **""Three matters admit no jest: divorce, marriage, and freeing.""**"
"7766","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported: A man came to ʿUmar and said, ""I divorced my wife irrevocably while she was menstruating."" ʿUmar said, ""You disobeyed your Lord and separated from your wife."" The man said, ""But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Ibn ʿUmar to take his wife back when he separated from her."" ʿUmar said to him, ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to take her back because a divorce remained by which he could do so, but nothing remains for you by which to take your wife back."""
"7767","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that he divorced his wife once while she was menstruating, then intended to follow it with two further pronouncements at the two remaining periods of purity. When that reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: > **""O Ibn ʿUmar, this is not how Allah commanded. You have erred against the Sunnah. The Sunnah is to face a period of purity and pronounce divorce once for each period.""** So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me, and I took her back. Then he said: > **""When she menstruates and then becomes pure, divorce her at that point or retain her.""** I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, if I had divorced her three times, would I still have the right to take her back?"" He said: > **""Then she would have become separated from you, and it would have been an act of disobedience.""**"
"7768","Abū al-Zubayr said: I asked Jābir about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating. He said, ""Ibn ʿUmar divorced his wife while she was menstruating. ʿUmar came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of that, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Let him take her back, for she is still his wife.""**"
"7769","Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ, who said to his wife: > **""I have divorced you; I have taken you back—this is not the divorce of the Muslims. Divorce a woman at the beginning of her purity.""**"
"7770","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: > **""There is no divorce except for the waiting period, and no freeing except for the sake of Allah.""**"
"7771","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: ""Divorce them for their waiting period."" ʿAbdullāh said, ""Divorce is in a period of purity without intercourse."""
"7772","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported: A slave boy of hers divorced his free wife twice. Umm Salamah sought a ruling from the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""She has become unlawful for him until she marries another husband.""**"
"7773","ʿAbdullāh رضي الله عنه said: Divorce is reckoned by men, and the waiting period is reckoned by women."
"7774","ʿAbdullāh رضي الله عنه said: If a man says to his wife, ""Your affair is in your hand,"" or ""Open your affair,"" or he grants her to her family and they accept her, it counts as one irrevocable divorce."
"7775","ʿAbdullāh رضي الله عنه said concerning the woman granted to her family: If they accept her, it counts as one divorce, and he has the greater right to her. If they do not accept her, it counts as nothing."
"7776","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: Declaring something unlawful requires the expiation of an oath."
"7777","In another narration: It is an oath, which he must expiate."
"7778","In another narration: If he intended divorce by it, it counts as divorce; otherwise it is an oath."
"7779","Al-Ḍaḥḥāk reported that ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنهما said: Declaring something unlawful requires the expiation of an oath."
"7780","ʿAbdullāh رضي الله عنه reported: He was with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه when a man and his wife came to him. The man said, ""I divorced my wife, then I took her back."" The wife said, ""Will you not allow me to relate the matter as it truly happened?"" ʿUmar said, ""Speak."" She said, ""He divorced me, then left me until the end of three menstrual cycles approached. My bleeding had stopped, I had laid out my washing water, closed my door, and removed my clothes. Then he knocked at the door and said, 'I have taken you back, I have taken you back.' So I abandoned my washing and put on my clothes."" ʿUmar said, ""What do you say concerning her, O son of the mother of ʿAbd?"" I said, ""I consider him to have the greater right to her, so long as prayer has not yet become lawful for her."" ʿUmar said, ""What an excellent view you have taken, and I hold the same."""
"7781","Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Masʿūd said: ʿUthmān sent to my father asking him about her. My father said, ""How can you give a ruling to a hypocrite?"" ʿUthmān said, ""We seek refuge with Allah from your being a hypocrite, and we seek refuge with Allah from such a case existing in Islam and then your passing away without clarifying it."" He said, ""I hold that he has the greater right to her until she washes from the third menstruation, when prayer becomes lawful for her."" I know of ʿUthmān only that he adopted that view."
"7782","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه said: My grandfather divorced a wife of his with a thousand divorces. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him. He said: > **""Did your grandfather not fear Allah? Three count for him, while nine hundred and ninety-seven are transgression and wrongdoing. If Allah wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him.""**"
"7783","ʿUbādah رضي الله عنه also reported in another narration: One of my forefathers divorced a wife a thousand times. His sons went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, our father divorced our mother a thousand times. Is there any way out for him?"" He said: > **""Your father did not fear Allah Almighty, so that Allah might make a way out for him. She is separated from him by three, contrary to the Sunnah, and nine hundred and ninety-seven are a sin upon his neck.""**"
"7784","ʿAlqamah said: A man came to Ibn Masʿūd and said, ""I divorced my wife ninety-nine times, and I asked and was told she is separated from me."" Ibn Masʿūd said, ""They wished to separate you from her."" He said, ""What do you say—may Allah have mercy on you?"" He thought he would grant him a concession. He said, ""Three separate her from you, and the rest are transgression."""
"7785","ʿAlqamah said: A man came to Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه and said, ""I divorced my wife as many times as the stars."" Ibn Masʿūd said something about the women of the family—a phrase I do not recall. Then another man came to him and said, ""I divorced my wife eight times."" Ibn Masʿūd said, ""Do these people wish her to be separated from you?"" He said, ""Yes."" Ibn Masʿūd said, ""O people, Allah has clarified divorce. Whoever divorces as Allah commanded him has clarified, but whoever confuses the matter, we cast his confusion back upon him. By Allah, you shall not confuse matters for yourselves while we bear it for you—meaning, it is as you say."""
"7786","ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said: Al-Zubayr struck Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr, so she cried out to ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, who came forward. When he saw him, he said, ""Your mother is divorced if you enter."" ʿAbdullāh said to him, ""Would you make my mother subject to your oath?"" Then he rushed in upon him and freed her, so she became separated from him. He said, ""I was but a boy then, and I would sometimes take hold of the hair of al-Zubayr's shoulders."""
"7787","Abū Usayd and Sahl ibn Saʿd رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us with some companions. We went out with him until we reached a garden called Al-Shawṭ. When we reached two walls there, we sat between them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Sit down.""** He entered, and the Jawnīyah was brought—she had been secluded in the house of Umaymah bint al-Nuʿmān ibn Shuraḥbīl among the palms—with a midwife alongside her. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her, he said: > **""Give yourself to me.""** She said, ""Would a queen give herself to a commoner?"" Then a woman of Banī al-Jawn called Umaymah said, ""I seek refuge with Allah from you."" He said: > **""You have sought refuge with the Mighty.""** Then he came out to us and said: > **""O Abū Usayd, clothe her with two linen garments and escort her to her family.""**"
"7788","Suwayd ibn Ghafalah said: ʿĀʾishah bint Khalīfah al-Khathʿamīyah was with al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī. When ʿAlī was struck and allegiance was given to al-Ḥasan for the caliphate, he entered upon her. She said, ""May the caliphate bring you joy."" He said to her, ""Do you show delight at the killing of ʿAlī? Go away, for you are divorced three times."" She wrapped herself in her covering and sat in a corner of the house, saying, ""By Allah, I did not mean what you took it to be."" She remained until her waiting period ended, then she moved away from him. He sent to her the remainder of her dowry due from him, along with a provision of ten thousand. When the messenger brought that to her, she said, ""A small provision from a beloved one who parts."" When the messenger returned to al-Ḥasan and told him what she said, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī wept and said, ""Had I not heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—or heard my father narrating from my grandfather that he said: > **""When a man divorces his wife three times at the periods of purity, or divorces her with three unspecified pronouncements, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband.""** I would have taken her back."""
"7789","Abū Isḥāq said: Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما granted a woman twenty thousand as provision. When I brought it and placed it before her, she said, ""A small provision from a beloved one who parts."""
"7790","In another narration: Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنهما granted two women twenty thousand and a skin of honey as provision. One of them—apparently Ḥunayfah—said, ""A small provision from a beloved one who parts."""
"7791","Anas رضي الله عنه reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who had a wife, divorced her three times, after which another man married her and divorced her before consummating with her—does she become lawful for her first husband? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""No, not until the second tastes of her honey what the first tasted, and she tastes of his honey.""**"
"7792","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr رضي الله عنهما reported: Rifāʿah ibn Simwāl divorced his wife. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān has married me, but with him is only like this""—gesturing to the fringe of her garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from her speech, then said to her: > **""Do you wish to return to Rifāʿah? No, not until you taste his honey and he tastes your honey.""**"
"7793","ʿUbaydullāh and al-Faḍl ibn al-ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: Al-Ghumayṣāʾ—or al-Rumayṣāʾ—came complaining of her husband to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, ""He does not approach her."" He said, ""She lies, O Messenger of Allah. Indeed I do so, but she wishes to return to her first husband."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""She is not lawful for him until he tastes her honey.""**"
"7794","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A woman divorced three times is not lawful for her first husband until she marries another husband, he consorts with her, and tastes of her honey.""**"
"7795","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: A woman of Banī Qurayẓah called Tamīmah was under ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr. He divorced her, and Rifāʿah of Banī Qurayẓah married her, then separated from her. She wished to return to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr, saying, ""O Messenger of Allah, there is nothing from him but like the fringe of this garment of mine."" He said: > **""By Allah, O Tamīmah, you shall not return to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān until another man besides him tastes your honey.""** She said, ""O Messenger of Allah, he came to me as a gift."""
"7796","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said concerning a woman divorced three times before consummation: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"7797","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه used to say: Intercourse by her master does not make her lawful for her husband."
"7798","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Al-ʿUsaylah means intercourse.""**"
"7799","In a narration with Abū Yaʿlā from ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها: The Prophet ﷺ by al-ʿUsaylah meant consummation."
"7800","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported: When the Prophet ﷺ gave his wives a choice, the one who chose herself was a woman of Banī Hilāl."
"7801","ʿAmr ibn Umayyah said: I heard men narrating from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""When a slave woman is freed, she has the choice so long as he has not had intercourse with her. If she wishes, she may separate from him; if he has had intercourse with her, she has no choice and cannot separate from him.""**"
"7802","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported: The husband of Barīrah was a black slave called Mughīth. I would see him following her through the streets of Madinah, weeping. The Prophet ﷺ gave four rulings concerning her: he ruled that the right of inheritance belongs to the one who frees, he gave her the choice, he commanded her to observe the waiting period of a free woman, and charity was once given to her, of which she gifted some to ʿĀʾishah. When she mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: > **""It is charity for her, and a gift to us.""**"
"7803","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: ʿĀʾishah wished to buy Barīrah and free her, but her masters said, ""No, unless you grant us the right of inheritance."" She mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: > **""Buy her and free her.""** Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition not in the Book of Allah, it is void.""** She was under a slave called Mughīth of Banī al-Mughīrah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted her the choice. Ibn ʿAbbās also narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made her waiting period that of a free woman."
"7804","Ibn Jurayj said: I was informed that Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said, ""If a slave woman under a slave is freed, does not know she has the choice, and does not choose until her husband is freed, or until he dies or she dies, they inherit from one another."""
"7805","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said concerning a slave woman sold while she has a husband: Her sale is her divorce."
"7806","Ubayy ibn Kaʿb رضي الله عنه said: I said to the Prophet ﷺ, ""'And for pregnant women, their term is until they deliver their burden' [Al-Ṭalāq: 4]—is this for the thrice-divorced woman or the widow?"" He said: > **""For the thrice-divorced woman and the widow.""**"
"7807","Ubayy ibn Kaʿb رضي الله عنه said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb disputed with me concerning the pregnant widow. I said, ""She may marry once she delivers."" Then Umm al-Ṭufayl, the mother of my child, said to ʿUmar and to me, ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Subayʿah al-Aslamīyah to marry once she delivered."""
"7808","Umm al-Ṭufayl, wife of Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, reported: She heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and Ubayy ibn Kaʿb disputing, so Umm al-Ṭufayl said, ""Why does ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb not ask Subayʿah al-Aslamīyah? Her husband died while she was pregnant, she delivered some days later, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her off."""
"7809","ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه reported: Subayʿah al-Aslamīyah bint al-Ḥārith delivered her burden fifteen nights after her husband's death. Abū al-Sanābil came to her and said, ""It seems you consider marrying? That is not for you until the later of the two terms passes."" She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him what Abū al-Sanābil had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Abū al-Sanābil has lied. When one comes to you whom you approve, bring him to me.""** Thus he informed her that her waiting period had ended."
"7810","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah reported concerning Subayʿah al-Aslamīyah bint al-Ḥārith the same narration or its like, with the words: > **""When a suitable match comes to you, come to me or inform me of him.""** Ibn Masʿūd was not mentioned in it."
"7811","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها said: A woman was divorced in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She remained twenty nights, then delivered her burden. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: > **""Seek good in your affair""** —meaning, marry."
"7812","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person beyond three days, except over a husband.""**"
"7813","ʿĀʾishah رضي الله عنها reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the waiting period of Barīrah that of a free woman."
"7814","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The widow is forbidden perfume and adornment."
"7815","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: If a woman is divorced and it is thought her menstruation has ceased, though it is not certain, she waits a year. If she does not menstruate in it, she observes three months after the year. If she menstruates during the three months, she reckons by menstruation. If she menstruates but it is incomplete after those three months following the year, she should not hasten until she knows whether her menstruation is complete or not."
"7816","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fāṭimah: > **""Move to Umm Sharīk, and do not deprive us of yourself.""**"
"7817","Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh رضي الله عنهما reported from his maternal aunt: She wished to go out to her palms to harvest them. A man said to her, ""That is not for you."" She came to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: > **""Go out and harvest your palms. Perhaps you will give charity or do good.""**"
"7818","ʿAlqamah said: Ibn Masʿūd was asked about women of Hamdān whose husbands' deaths were announced to them. They said, ""We feel lonely."" ʿAbdullāh said, ""They may gather by day, then each one returns to her house by night."""
"7819","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ: At Awṭās he forbade a man to have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she delivers."
"7820","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade, on the day of Ḥunayn, selling the fifth before it is divided, and approaching women until they deliver what is in their wombs, if they are pregnant."
"7821","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade approaching a pregnant woman until she delivers."
"7822","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: A slave woman is declared free of pregnancy by one menstruation."
"7823","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr and Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah رضي الله عنهما said: Ḥabībah bint Sahl was under Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shimās al-Anṣārī. She disliked him, for he was an unsightly man. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I see him—were it not for fear of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, I would have spat in his face."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Will you return to him the garden he gave you as dowry?""** She said, ""Yes."" He sent for him; she returned his garden to him, and he separated them. That was the first khulʿ in Islam."
"7824","Anas رضي الله عنه said: The wife of Thābit ibn Shimās—that is, Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shimās—came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke words as though she disliked him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Will you return his garden to him?""** She said, ""Yes."" So the Prophet ﷺ sent to Thābit: > **""Take that from her and divorce her.""**"
"7825","ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Women who seek khulʿ and wrench themselves away—they are the hypocrites.""**"
"7826","Ibn Abī Mulaykah said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, ʿIkrimah ibn Abī Jahl fled and boarded the sea. The sea grew rough with them, so the sailors and those at sea began calling upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and seeking His aid. He said, ""What is this?"" It was said, ""This is a place where none benefits except Allah, Mighty and Majestic."" ʿIkrimah said, ""Then this is the God of Muḥammad to whom he calls us. Turn us back."" So they returned, he came back and accepted Islam. His wife had accepted Islam before him, so they remained upon their marriage."
"7827","Al-Shaʿbī reported: Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, accepted Islam while her husband Abū al-ʿĀṣ ibn al-Rabīʿ was a polytheist. He accepted Islam some time after that, and they did not renew their marriage."
"7828","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: In the Jāhilīyah, when a man said to his wife, ""You are to me as my mother's back,"" she became unlawful for him. The first to practice ẓihār in Islam was a man whose wife was his cousin, called Khuwaylah. He made ẓihār from her, then regretted it, saying, ""You have become unlawful for me."" She said the like to him. He said, ""Go to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him."" She came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining to him, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: ""Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah"" [Al-Mujādalah: 1] up to His saying: ""the freeing of a slave before they touch one another"" [Al-Mujādalah: 3]. She said, ""I am but one person—he has none besides me."" He said, ""Then fasting two consecutive months."" She said, ""By Allah, he drinks three times a day."" He said, ""Then feeding sixty poor persons."" She said, ""By my father and mother, it is but one meal to the next—we can afford nothing else."" So the Prophet ﷺ called for half a wasq—thirty ṣāʿs, a wasq being sixty ṣāʿs—and said: > **""Let him feed sixty poor persons with it, and take you back.""**"
"7829","Abū Salamah and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān reported: Salmān ibn Ṣakhr al-Bayāḍī made his wife as his mother's back upon him if he approached her until Ramaḍān passed. When half of Ramaḍān passed, she grew healthy and full, pleasing him, so he approached her by night. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that. He said: > **""Free a slave.""** He said, ""I cannot find one."" He said: > **""Fast two consecutive months.""** He said, ""I cannot."" He said: > **""Feed sixty poor persons.""** He said, ""I cannot find the means."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a basket containing fifteen or sixteen ṣāʿs of dates. He said: > **""Take this and give it in charity to sixty poor persons.""**"
"7830","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: Ẓihār in the Jāhilīyah made women unlawful. The first ẓihār in Islam was by Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit, whose wife was Khuwaylah bint Khuwaylid. The man was weak, and the woman was strong-bodied. When he uttered ẓihār, he said, ""I see you have become unlawful for me. Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—perhaps you will find something that returns you to me."" She went, while he sat waiting for her by the sides of the well. She came to the Prophet ﷺ while a woman combing his hair was dressing it, and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, Aws ibn al-Ṣāmit—whose weakness of judgment and incapacity you know—has made ẓihār from me. None deserves kindness toward him more than I, if kindness is to be shown, and he has made ẓihār from me, O Messenger of Allah. I seek something that returns me to him, may my father and mother be ransomed for you."" He said: > **""O Khuwaylah, we have not been commanded anything concerning your affair; if we are commanded, I shall inform you.""** While the hairdresser had finished one side of his head and begun the other, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down revelation. When revelation descended upon him, his face would flush, until he felt its coolness; when it lifted, his face returned white as silver. Then he spoke what he had been commanded by revelation. His hairdresser said, ""O Khuwaylah, I think it is now concerning your affair."" She trembled and said, ""O Allah, I seek refuge with You from anything but good descending upon me, for I sought nothing from Your Messenger but good."" When it lifted from him, he said: > **""O Khuwaylah, Allah has sent down concerning you and your companion.""** Then he recited: ""Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah, and Allah hears your dialogue"" [Al-Mujādalah: 1] up to His saying: ""then freeing a slave before they touch one another."" She said, ""O Messenger of Allah, he has no servant besides me, and I have none besides him."" He recited: ""Whoever cannot find this, then fasting two consecutive months."" She said, ""By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, if he does not eat twice a day, his sight weakens."" He recited: ""Whoever cannot do that, then feeding sixty poor persons."" She said, ""By Allah, today we have no such means."" He said: > **""Tell him to go to so-and-so, take half a wasq of dates from him, give it in charity to sixty poor persons, and take you back.""** She returned, and when he saw her he asked, ""What happened?"" She said, ""Good—you are poor, and you have been commanded to go to so-and-so, take half a wasq from him, give it in charity to sixty poor persons, and take me back."" So he hastened, brought the dates—though before that, in his weakness, he could not carry five ṣāʿs upon his back."
"7831","Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept away from his wives—Shuʿbah said, ""I think he said: a month."" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb رضي الله عنه came to him while he was in an upper room upon a mat that had marked his back. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah, Khosrow drinks from silver and gold, while you are like this?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Their good things have been hastened for them in the life of this world.""** Then the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The month is thus and thus.""** And he folded the thumb on the third time—twenty-nine days."
"7832","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: I wished to ask ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, ""If you two support one another against him"" [Al-Taḥrīm: 4], but I held him in awe. When we performed Ḥajj with him, I said, ""If I do not ask him during this Ḥajj, I shall never ask him."" When we completed our Ḥajj, I caught up with him at Baṭn Marr, where he had stayed behind for some need. He said, ""Welcome, O cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—what is your need?"" I said, ""Something I wished to ask you about, O Commander of the Faithful, but I held you in awe."" He said, ""Ask me whatever you wish, for we knew nothing until we learned it."" I said, ""Tell me about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, 'If you two support one another against him'—who are they?"" He said, ""You ask none more knowledgeable of that than me. When we were in Makkah, none of us spoke with his wife—she was but a servant of the house; when he had a need, he took her by the foot and fulfilled his need. When we came to Madinah, our wives learned from the women of the Anṣār, and began speaking to us and answering us back. I once ordered some servants of mine concerning a need, and my wife said, 'Rather do such-and-such.' I rose toward her with a stick and struck her with it. She said, 'How strange you are, O son of al-Khaṭṭāb! You wish not to be spoken to, yet the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ speak to him!' So I went out and entered upon Ḥafṣah, saying, 'O my daughter, beware speaking to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or asking him, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has neither dinar nor dirham to give you. Whatever need you have—even oil for your head—ask me for it.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Fajr, he would sit in his prayer place with the people around him until the sun rose, then enter upon his wives one by one, greeting them and supplicating for them, staying with whichever one's day it was. Once Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar was gifted a vial of honey from Ṭāʾif. When the Prophet ﷺ entered and greeted her, she detained him and gave him honey to eat or drink. ʿĀʾishah was troubled that he stayed with her, so she told her Abyssinian slave girl Khaḍrāʾ, 'When the Prophet ﷺ visits Ḥafṣah, go and see what he does.' The girl told ʿĀʾishah that he drinks honey there. ʿĀʾishah sent word to her companions, saying, 'When the Prophet ﷺ comes to you, say: we smell maghāfīr upon you.' When the Prophet ﷺ came to ʿĀʾishah, she said, 'O Messenger of Allah, have you eaten anything today? I smell maghāfīr upon you.' He disliked any odor being perceived from him, and said: > **""It was only honey. By Allah, I shall never eat it again.""** When Ḥafṣah's day came, she said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have business with my father—my allowance is with him; if you permit me, I shall go to him.' He permitted her. Then the Prophet ﷺ sent for his slave girl Māriyah, who came to Ḥafṣah's house, and he was intimate with her there. Ḥafṣah returned meanwhile to find the door closed, and sat at the door. When the Prophet ﷺ came out, she said, 'O Messenger of Allah, in my house and upon my bed?' He said: > **""She is unlawful for me. Do not mention this to anyone.""** She mentioned it to ʿĀʾishah. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you' [Al-Taḥrīm: 1]. By the two, He meant ʿĀʾishah and Ḥafṣah—people said the two concealed nothing from one another. Then ʿUmar said: I had a brother among the Anṣār—when I attended and he was absent at his estate, I told him what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and when I was absent at my estate, he told me. One day he came to me—while we feared Jabalah ibn al-Ayham al-Ghassānī—and said, 'Do you know what has happened?' I said, 'What? Perhaps Jabalah ibn al-Ayham al-Ghassānī approaches?' He said, 'No, but worse than that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Fajr but did not sit as he used to sit, nor visit his wives as he used to do. He has secluded himself in his upper room, leaving the people in turmoil, not knowing his affair.' So I came while the people in the mosque were in turmoil, unknowing. I said, 'O people, stay as you are.' Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his upper room, for which a ladder had been set, and climbed it. I said to his black servant who guarded him, 'Seek permission for ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.' He sought permission for me, and I entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in his upper room with a mat, hanging skins, his side bare against the mat so that it marked his side, and beneath his head a pillow of leather stuffed with fiber. When I saw him, I wept. He said: > **""What makes you weep?""** I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Persia and Rome—one of them reclines upon brocade and silk!' He said: > **""Their good things have been hastened for them, and the Hereafter is for us.""** I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is your affair? I left the people in turmoil awaiting word from you.' He said: > **""I have secluded myself from them.""** I said, 'Have you divorced them?' He said: > **""No, but something arose between me and my wives, so I wished not to enter upon them for a month.""** Then I went out to the people, saying, 'O people, return, for there is a matter between the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his wives, and he wished seclusion.' Then I entered upon Ḥafṣah, saying, 'O my daughter, do you speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, anger him, and show jealousy toward him?' She said, 'I shall never again speak to him of anything he dislikes.' Then I entered upon Umm Salamah—she was my maternal aunt—saying to her as I said to Ḥafṣah. She said, 'How strange you are, O ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb! You speak on every matter, until you wish to come between the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his wives! What prevents us from being jealous over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when your own wives are jealous over you?' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'O Prophet, say to your wives: if you desire the life of this world and its adornment, come, I shall provide for you and release you with a gracious release' [Al-Aḥzāb: 28] to its end."
"7833","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: The īlāʾ of the Jāhilīyah was a year or two years. Then Allah set a term for īlāʾ: whoever's īlāʾ is less than four months is not īlāʾ."
"7834","Abū Mūsā رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning one who makes īlāʾ from his wife: > **""If he wishes, he may take her back within the four months; if he resolves upon divorce, then upon her is what is upon a divorced woman of waiting.""**"
"7835","Ibrāhīm reported: A man called ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays made īlāʾ from his wife. Four months passed before he had intercourse with her; then he had intercourse with her after the four months, forgetting his oath. He came to ʿAlqamah ibn Qays and mentioned that to him. They both came to Ibn Masʿūd and asked him. He said, ""She is separated from you—propose to her anew."" So he proposed to her anew and gave her a ritl of silver as dowry."
"7836","Wabarah reported from a man of his people: He made īlāʾ from his wife for ten days, then asked Ibn Masʿūd about it. He said, ""When four months pass, it is īlāʾ."""
"7837","ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad reported: A cousin of his made īlāʾ from his wife for ten days, then went out. He returned after four months had passed and was intimate with his wife. He met a man who reminded him of his oath. He came to Ibn Masʿūd and asked him. He made him swear by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that he had not known, then sent to his wife and made her swear by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, that she had not known. Then he commanded him to propose to her anew."
"7838","Abū Qilābah said: Al-Nuʿmān made īlāʾ from his wife while sitting with Ibn Masʿūd. He struck his thigh and said, ""When four months pass, acknowledge one divorce."""
"7839","Qatādah reported that ʿAlī, Ibn ʿAbbās, and Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنهم said: When the four months pass, it is one divorce, and she has the greater right to herself. ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd said: she observes the waiting period of a divorced woman."
"7840","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: When ""Those who accuse chaste women and then do not bring four witnesses—flog them eighty lashes, never accept their testimony, and they are the defiantly disobedient"" [Al-Nūr: 4] was revealed, Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, the chief of the Anṣār, said, ""Was it revealed thus, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O company of Anṣār, do you not hear what your chief says?""** They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, do not blame him, for he is a jealous man. By Allah, he never married any woman but a virgin, nor ever divorced any woman but that none of us dared marry her, from the intensity of his jealousy."" Saʿd said, ""By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I know it is true and from Allah, but I marvel: if I found a vile man with my wife, I would have no right to rouse him or move him until I bring four witnesses—by Allah, I would not bring them until he had fulfilled his need?!"" Only a short while passed before Hilāl ibn Umayyah came—one of the three whose repentance was accepted. He came from his land by night, found a man with his wife, saw with his eyes and heard with his ears, yet did not rouse him until morning. In the morning he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, ""O Messenger of Allah, I came to my wife by night and found a man with her. I saw with my eyes and heard with my ears."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what he brought and it weighed heavily upon him. The Anṣār gathered, saying, ""We are now tried by what Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah said—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will now flog Hilāl ibn Umayyah and nullify his testimony among the Muslims."" He said, ""By Allah, I hope Allah will make a way out for me."" Hilāl said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I see what I brought weighs heavily upon you, but by Allah, I am truthful."" While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to order his flogging, revelation descended upon him—when it descended, they recognized it by the flushing of his skin—so they held back until the revelation ended. Then ""Those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves"" [Al-Nūr: 6] was revealed, and he mentioned the rest of the narration."
"7841","Ḥudhayfah رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""O Abū Bakr, what would you do if you found a man with Umm Rūmān?""** He said, ""I would do evil to him."" Then he said: > **""O ʿUmar, what would you do if you found a man—what would you do?""** He said, ""By Allah, I would kill him."" He said: > **""And you, O Suhayl ibn Bayḍāʾ?""** He said, ""May Allah curse the wretch—he is vile; may Allah curse the wretched woman—she is vile; and may Allah curse the first of the three who mentioned it."" He said: > **""O son of Bayḍāʾ, you have interpreted the Qurʾān: 'Those who accuse their wives' to the end of the verse.""**"
"7842","ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī رضي الله عنه reported: He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when this verse was revealed: ""then do not bring four witnesses"" [Al-Nūr: 4]. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah—until they bring four witnesses, the vile one will already have fulfilled his need?!"" He had hardly risen before his cousin, his paternal uncle's son, came with his wife carrying an infant, she saying, ""He is from you,"" and he saying, ""He is not from me."" Then the verse of liʿān was revealed. He said, ""I am the first to speak of it and the first to be tried by it."""
"7843","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما said: A man of the Anṣār married a woman of Balʿajlān. He spent the night with her; in the morning he found she was not a virgin. Their case was raised to the Prophet ﷺ, who summoned the girl. She said, ""Indeed I was a virgin."" So he commanded them both, and they performed liʿān, and he gave her the dowry."
"7844","Al-Ṭabarānī said: Khawlah bint ʿĀṣim, the woman of liʿān, is the one between whom and her husband the Prophet ﷺ effected separation."
"7845","Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنهما said, ""If her husband accuses her and has divorced her with a divorce in which he retains the right of return, they perform liʿān. If he accused her after divorcing her irrevocably, he does not perform liʿān with her."""
"7846","Ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: The two who perform liʿān never reunite, ever."
"7847","Saʿd ibn Maʿbad reported: Yuḥannas and Ṣafīyah were of the fifth. She bore a boy, claimed by both the adulterer and Yuḥannas. They disputed before ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, who referred them to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib. ʿAlī عليه السلام said, ""I judge herein by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.""** And he flogged her fifty and fifty."""
"7848","Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ رضي الله عنه reported: The Prophet ﷺ ruled the child for the bed."
"7849","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.""**"
"7850","Al-Ḥasan said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"7851","The daughter of Zamʿah said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""My father died leaving his umm walad. We suspected her of a man, and she bore a child resembling the man we suspected her of."" He said to her: > **""As for you, veil yourself from him, for he is not your brother—but he has inheritance.""**"
"7852","Zaynab al-Asadīyah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, my father died leaving a slave girl who bore a boy, and we suspected her."" He said: > **""Bring him to me.""** When they brought him, he looked at him, then said to her: > **""Inheritance is his, but as for you, veil yourself from him.""**"
"7853","Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq said: Naṣr ibn al-Ḥajjāj ibn ʿIlāṭ al-Sulamī claimed ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabāḥ, freedman of Khālid ibn al-Walīd. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Khālid ibn al-Walīd rose, saying, ""My freedman, born upon my master's bed."" Naṣr said, ""My brother enjoined me concerning his station."" Their dispute lengthened, so they entered with him before Muʿāwiyah—with Fihr beneath his head—and both made their claims. Muʿāwiyah said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.""** Naṣr said, ""Then where is this judgment of yours, O Muʿāwiyah, concerning Ziyād?"" Muʿāwiyah said, ""The judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than the judgment of Muʿāwiyah."" ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabāḥ would not concede to Naṣr's claim, so Naṣr spoke verses: ""O Abā Khālid, take wealth like mine as inheritance, and take me as a brother, a witness in calamities. O Abā Khālid, my wealth is abundance and rank, captives and lineages that stir you onward. O Abā Khālid, do not make our daughters slaves to Makhzūm, though they be wealthy. O Abā Khālid, if you fear the son of Khālid, al-Ḥajjāj never feared Khālid. O Abā Khālid, neither are we fire nor they gardens in which you see still springs."""
"7854","Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.""**"
"7855","Al-Barāʾ and Zayd ibn Arqam رضي الله عنهما said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Ghadīr Khumm, shielding his head from the branches of the tree. He said: > **""Charity is not lawful for me nor for my household. May Allah curse whoever claims descent from other than his father, and may Allah curse whoever allies with other than his masters. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. There is no bequest for an heir.""**"
"7856","Al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The child belongs to the bed.""**"
"7857","Ibn al-Zubayr رضي الله عنهما reported from the Prophet ﷺ: He granted the son of the slave girl of Zamʿah inheritance, because he was born upon the bed of Zamʿah."
"7858","ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit رضي الله عنه said: Among the judgments of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is that the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"7859","Abū Masʿūd رضي الله عنه said: I was before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the Greater Ḥajj, the foam of his she-camel falling upon my back. I heard him say: > **""Give every rightful one his right. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever allies with other than his masters, or claims descent from other than his father—upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither obligatory nor voluntary deed is accepted from him.""**"
"7860","Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone. A woman may not dispose of anything of her wealth except with her husband's permission.""**"
"7861","Abū Wāʾil reported that ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥudhāfah said, ""O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?"" He said: > **""Your father is Ḥudhāfah. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.""** He said, ""Had you attributed me even to an Abyssinian, I would have followed him."" His mother said, ""You have exposed me."" He said, ""I wished to find rest."""
"7862","Ibn ʿUmar رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever disowns his child in order to disgrace him in this world, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before all witnesses—requital for requital.""**"
"7863","Muʿādh ibn Anas رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: > **""Allah Almighty has servants to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, nor look at them.""** It was said, ""Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: > **""One who disowns his parents and turns away from them, one who disowns his child, and a man upon whom a people bestowed favor, yet he denied their favor and disowned them.""**"
